      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "A metal-free [2+2] cycloaddition and 1,4-addition sequence induced by S-centered radicals has been achieved by treating benzene-linked allene-ynes with aryldiazonium tetrafluoroborates and DABCO-bis(sulfur dioxide) in a one-pot procedure. The reaction provides a greener and more practical access to functionalized cyclobuta[a]naphthalen-4-ols with valuable applications. More than 50 examples are demonstrated with excellent diastereoselectivity and chemical yields. The reaction pathway is proposed to proceed by the following steps:[2+2] cycloaddition, insertion of SO2 , 1,4-addition, diazotization, and tautomerization."
      },
